<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<usx version="3.1">
<book code="HOS" style="id">BLB-Draft</book>

<para style="h">Hosea</para>

<para style="toc1">Hosea</para>

<para style="rem">sourceUrl=https://literalbible.com/blb.docx fetchedAtUtc=2026-09-01T15:43:00Z status=draft id=BLB-Draft spec=USFM-USX 3.1.1 char:add=docx-italic note:f=docx-footnotes note:x=docx-heading-crossrefs</para>

<chapter number="1" style="c" sid="HOS 1"/>

<para style="s">Hosea’s Wife and Children</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="HOS 1:1"/>The word of YHWH that came to Hosea son of Beeri in the days of Uzziah, Jotham, Ahaz, <char style="add">and</char> Hezekiah, kings of Judah, and in the days of Jeroboam son of Joash,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Joash</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is a variant of </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Jehoash</char></note> king of Israel. <verse eid="HOS 1:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="HOS 1:2"/>The beginning when YHWH <char style="add">first</char> spoke by Hosea, YHWH said to Hosea, “Go take for yourself a wife of prostitution, and children of prostitution, for the land is flagrantly prostituting itself from after YHWH!” <verse eid="HOS 1:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="HOS 1:3"/>And he went and took Gomer the daughter of Diblaim; and she conceived and bore to him a son. <verse eid="HOS 1:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="HOS 1:4"/>And YHWH said to him: “Call his name Jezreel;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Jezreel</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">God sows</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verse 11.</char></note> for yet a little and I will avenge the bloodshed of Jezreel on the house of Jehu, and I will bring to an end the kingdom of the house of Israel. <verse eid="HOS 1:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="HOS 1:5"/>And it will come to pass in that day <char style="add">that</char> I will break the bow of Israel in the valley of Jezreel.” <verse eid="HOS 1:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="HOS 1:6"/>And <char style="add">his wife</char> conceived again, and she bore a daughter. And He said to him: “Call her name Lo-ruhamah,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Lo-ruhamah</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">she has not received mercy</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> for no longer will I continue <char style="add">to</char> have compassion on the house of Israel, that I should ever lift the for them. <verse eid="HOS 1:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="HOS 1:7"/>And <char style="add">on</char> the house of Judah I will have compassion, and I will save them, by YHWH their God; I will not save them by bow, or by sword, or by battle, by horses, or by horsemen.” <verse eid="HOS 1:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="HOS 1:8"/>And she had weaned Lo-ruhamah, and she conceived and bore a son. <verse eid="HOS 1:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="HOS 1:9"/>And He said, “Call his name Lo-ammi,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Lo-ammi</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">not My people</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> for you⁺ <char style="add">are</char> not My people, and I am not unto you⁺! <verse eid="HOS 1:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="HOS 1:10"/>And the number of the sons of Israel shall be like the sand of the sea, which cannot be measured and cannot be counted; and it will come to pass, in the place where it was said to them, ‘You⁺ <char style="add">are</char> not My people,’ it will be said of them, ‘Sons of the living God.’ <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Romans 9:26</char></note><verse eid="HOS 1:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="HOS 1:11"/>And the sons of Judah and the sons of Israel will be gathered together, and they will appoint for themselves one head, and they will go up from the land, for great <char style="add">will be</char> the day of Jezreel. <verse eid="HOS 1:11"/></para>

<chapter eid="HOS 1"/>

<chapter number="2" style="c" sid="HOS 2"/>

<para style="s">Israel’s Adultery Rebuked</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="HOS 2:1"/><char style="add">“</char> Say of your⁺ brothers, ‘Ammi,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Ammi</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">my people</char></note>’ </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:1">and of your⁺ sisters, ‘Ruhamah.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Ruhamah</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">she has received mercy</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Mercy is shown</char></note>’ <verse eid="HOS 2:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="HOS 2:2"/>Plead with your⁺ mother—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:2">plead, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 2:2">for she <char style="add">is</char> not My wife, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:2">and I <char style="add">am</char> not her Husband—</para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 2:2">that she might turn aside her prostitution from her face, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:2">and her adultery from between her breasts, <verse eid="HOS 2:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="HOS 2:3"/>lest I strip her naked, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:3">and expose her like the day of her being born, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 2:3">and make her like the desert, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:3">and set her like a parched land, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:3">and kill her with thirst! <verse eid="HOS 2:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="HOS 2:4"/>And I will not show compassion <char style="add">to</char> her children, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:4">for they <char style="add">are</char> sons of prostitution. <verse eid="HOS 2:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="HOS 2:5"/>For their mother has been a prostitute; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:5">she who conceived them has acted shamefully, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 2:5">for she said, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:5">‘I will go after my lovers, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 2:5">those giving <char style="add">me</char> my bread and my water, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:5">my wool and my linen, my oil and my drink.’ <verse eid="HOS 2:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="HOS 2:6"/>Therefore, behold, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:6">I am hedging up your path with thorns; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 2:6">and I will wall her up with a wall, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:6">so her paths she cannot find. <verse eid="HOS 2:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="HOS 2:7"/>And she will pursue her lovers, and she will not overtake them; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:7">she will seek them, and she will not find <char style="add">them</char>. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 2:7">She will say, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:7">‘I will go and return to my first husband, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:7">for <char style="add">it was</char> better for me then than now!’ <verse eid="HOS 2:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="HOS 2:8"/>And she did not know </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:8">that I gave to her the grain, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:8">and the new wine, and the oil, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 2:8">and multiplied for her silver and gold, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:8"><char style="add">which</char> they prepared for Baal. <verse eid="HOS 2:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="HOS 2:9"/>Therefore I will return, and I will take away My grain in its time, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:9">and My new wine in its season; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 2:9">and I will snatch away My wool and My linen </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:9">to cover her nakedness! <verse eid="HOS 2:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="HOS 2:10"/>And now I will uncover her lewdness </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:10">before the eyes of her lovers, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 2:10">and no man will deliver her </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:10">from My hand. <verse eid="HOS 2:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="HOS 2:11"/>And I will make cease all her rejoicing—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:11">her feast, her New Moon, and her Sabbath, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:11">and all her appointed feasts. <verse eid="HOS 2:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="HOS 2:12"/>And I will destroy her vines and her fig trees, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:12">of which she has said, “My wages, they <char style="add">are</char> for me that which my lovers have given to me.” </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 2:12">I will make them a forest, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:12">and the beasts of the field will devour them. <verse eid="HOS 2:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="HOS 2:13"/>And I will visit punishment on her for the days of the Baals, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:13">to which she burned incense </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 2:13">and adorned herself with her rings and jewelry, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:13">and went after her lovers—</para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 2:13">and Me she forgot,” </para>

<para style="qs" vid="HOS 2:13">a declaration of YHWH. <verse eid="HOS 2:13"/></para>

<para style="s">God’s Mercy to Israel</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="HOS 2:14"/>“Therefore, behold, I am enticing her, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:14">and I will bring her into the desert, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:14">and I have spoken upon her heart. <verse eid="HOS 2:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="HOS 2:15"/>And I will give to her her vineyards from there, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:15">and the valley of Achor<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Achor</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">trouble</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:15">as a door of hope; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 2:15">and she will sing there </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:15">as in the days of her youth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:15">and as in the day of her coming up from the land of Egypt. <verse eid="HOS 2:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="HOS 2:16"/>And it will come to pass on that day, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:16">a declaration of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 2:16">“<char style="add">That</char> you will call out ‘My Ishi,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">My Ishi</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">My husband</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note>’ </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:16">and no longer will you call Me ‘My Baal.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">My Baal</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">My master</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">My lord</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note>’ <verse eid="HOS 2:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="HOS 2:17"/>For I will take the names of the Baals from her mouth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:17">and no longer will they be remembered by their name. <verse eid="HOS 2:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="HOS 2:18"/>And I will make for them a covenant on that day, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:18">with the beasts of the field and with the birds of the heavens, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:18">and <char style="add">with</char> the creeping things of the ground. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 2:18">And bow and sword and battle </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:18">I will break off from the earth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:18">and I will make them lie down in safety. <verse eid="HOS 2:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="HOS 2:19"/>And I will betroth you to Me forever; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:19">and I will betroth you to Me in righteousness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:19">and in justice, and with loving devotion,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Forms of the Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">chesed</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> are translated here and in most cases throughout the Scriptures as </char><char style="fq" closed="false">loving devotion</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; the range of meaning includes </char><char style="fq" closed="false">love</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">goodness</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">kindness</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">faithfulness</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, and </char><char style="fq" closed="false">mercy</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, as well as </char><char style="fq" closed="false">loyalty to a covenant</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> and with compassion. <verse eid="HOS 2:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="HOS 2:20"/>And I will betroth you to Me in faithfulness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:20">and you will know YHWH. <verse eid="HOS 2:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="HOS 2:21"/>And it will come to pass in that day <char style="add">that</char> I will answer,” </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:21">a declaration of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 2:21">“I will answer the heavens, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:21">and they will answer the earth; <verse eid="HOS 2:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="HOS 2:22"/>and the earth will answer with the grain, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:22">and with the new wine, and with the oil; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:22">and they will answer Jezreel,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Jezreel</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">God sows</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> <verse eid="HOS 2:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="HOS 2:23"/>and I will sow her for Myself in the land, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:23">and I will show compassion <char style="add">to</char> ‘Lo-ruhama;’ </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 2:23">and I will say <char style="add">to</char> ‘Lo-ammi,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.23 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Lo-ruhamah</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">she has not received mercy</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">I will love her who was not loved</char></note>’ </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:23">‘You <char style="add">are</char> My people,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.23 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Lo-ammi</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">not My people</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note>’ </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 2:23">and he will say, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 2:23">‘My God.’” <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.23 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Romans 9:25 and 1 Peter 2:10</char></note><verse eid="HOS 2:23"/></para>

<chapter eid="HOS 2"/>

<chapter number="3" style="c" sid="HOS 3"/>

<para style="s">Hosea Redeems His Wife</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="HOS 3:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Zechariah 2:6–13</char></note>And YHWH said to me: “Again go, love a woman loved by by another and is committing adultery, according to the love of YHWH <char style="add">for</char> the sons of Israel, and they are turning to other gods and are loving the cakes of raisins!” <verse eid="HOS 3:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="HOS 3:2"/>And I bought her for myself with fifteen <char style="add">shekels</char> of silver<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">15 shekels</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 6 ounces or 171 grams of silver.</char></note> and a homer of barley and a lethech of barley.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">a homer and a half of barley</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; that is, a total of approximately 9.36 bushels or 330 liters (probably about 436 pounds or 198 kilograms of barley); LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">a homer of barley and a wineskin full of wine</char></note> <verse eid="HOS 3:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="HOS 3:3"/>And I said to her: “Many days you will dwell with me; you will not act like a prostitute, and you will not be unto a man; I also toward you.” <verse eid="HOS 3:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="HOS 3:4"/>For many days the sons of Israel will dwell without king or prince, and without sacrifice or sacred pillar, and without ephod or teraphim. <verse eid="HOS 3:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="HOS 3:5"/>Afterward the sons of Israel will return, and they will seek YHWH their God and David their king, and they will come trembling to YHWH and to His goodness in the latter days. <verse eid="HOS 3:5"/></para>

<chapter eid="HOS 3"/>

<chapter number="4" style="c" sid="HOS 4"/>

<para style="s">God’s Case against His People</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="HOS 4:1"/>Hear the word of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:1">O sons of Israel, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 4:1">for a case <char style="add">is</char> unto YHWH </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:1">against those dwelling in the land: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 4:1">“For there is no truth, and there is no loving devotion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:1">and there is no knowledge of God in the land. <verse eid="HOS 4:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="HOS 4:2"/>Cursing, and lying, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:2">and killing, and stealing, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 4:2">and committing adultery, they break all restraint, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:2">and bloodshed touches upon bloodshed. <verse eid="HOS 4:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="HOS 4:3"/>Upon thus mourns the land, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:3">and languish all dwelling in it; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 4:3">with the beasts of the field and the birds of the heavens, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:3">and even the fish of the sea, they are gathered up. <verse eid="HOS 4:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="HOS 4:4"/>Only let no man contend </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:4">and no man rebuke, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 4:4">for your people <char style="add">are</char> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:4">like those who contend with a priest.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">for My case is against you, O priests</char></note> <verse eid="HOS 4:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="HOS 4:5"/>And you will stumble by day, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:5">and will stumble also the prophet with you by night, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:5">and I will destroy your mother. <verse eid="HOS 4:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="HOS 4:6"/>My people are destroyed </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:6">for lack of knowledge, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 4:6">because you have rejected knowledge, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:6">and I will reject you from being priest unto Me; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 4:6">and you have forgotten the law of your God; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:6">I will forget your children also. <verse eid="HOS 4:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="HOS 4:7"/>According to their becoming numerous, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:7">so they sinned against Me; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 4:7">their Glory they exchanged<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">they exchanged their glorious God</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> (Syriac); MT </char><char style="fq" closed="false">I will exchange their glory</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:7">for shame. <verse eid="HOS 4:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="HOS 4:8"/>The sin<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the sin offerings</char></note> of My people they eat up, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:8">and toward their iniquity they lift up their soul. <verse eid="HOS 4:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="HOS 4:9"/>And it will be </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:9">like people, like priest; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 4:9">and I will visit punishment on them for their ways, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:9">and their deeds I will repay to them. <verse eid="HOS 4:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="HOS 4:10"/>For they will eat, and they will not be satisfied; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:10">they will prostitute themselves and not increase, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:10">because they have abandoned to give heed to YHWH. <verse eid="HOS 4:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="HOS 4:11"/>Prostitution and wine and new wine </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:11">take the heart. <verse eid="HOS 4:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="HOS 4:12"/>My people consult with a piece of wood, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:12">and their staff declares <char style="add">it</char> to them; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 4:12">for the spirit of prostitution has led them astray, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:12">and they have prostituted themselves from under their God. <verse eid="HOS 4:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="HOS 4:13"/>On the tops of the mountains they sacrifice, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:13">and on the hills they burn incense, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 4:13">under oak and poplar and terebinth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:13">because its shade <char style="add">is</char> good. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 4:13">In this <char style="add">way</char> your⁺ daughters prostitute themselves, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:13">and your⁺ brides commit adultery. <verse eid="HOS 4:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="HOS 4:14"/>I will not visit punishment on your⁺ daughters </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:14">when they prostitute themselves, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 4:14">or on your⁺ brides </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:14">when they commit adultery; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 4:14">for they themselves go off with the prostitutes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:14">and offer sacrifices with shrine prostitutes, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 4:14">and a people without understanding </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:14">will be thrown down. <verse eid="HOS 4:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="HOS 4:15"/>Though you prostitute yourself, O Israel, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:15">do not let Judah become guilty; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 4:15">and do not come to Gilgal, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:15">and do not go up <char style="add">to</char> Beth-Aven, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 4:15">and do not swear an oath, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:15">‘As YHWH lives.’ <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Beth-aven</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">house of wickedness</char><char style="ft" closed="false">. This is a derogatory term for Bethel, which means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">house of God</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see 1 Kings 12:28–29.</char></note><verse eid="HOS 4:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="HOS 4:16"/>For being stubborn like a heifer, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:16">Israel is stubborn; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 4:16">now will YHWH let them graze </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:16">like a lamb in a broad pasture? <verse eid="HOS 4:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="HOS 4:17"/>Ephraim<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, the northern kingdom of Israel</char></note> is joined to idols; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:17">leave him alone! <verse eid="HOS 4:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="HOS 4:18"/>Has turned aside their liquor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:18">they engage in flagrant prostitution; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:18">her rulers<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.18 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">her shields</char></note> dearly love love dishonor. <verse eid="HOS 4:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="HOS 4:19"/>The wind has constrained her<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">has wrapped her</char></note> in its wings, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 4:19">and they will be ashamed of their sacrifices. <verse eid="HOS 4:19"/></para>

<chapter eid="HOS 4"/>

<chapter number="5" style="c" sid="HOS 5"/>

<para style="s">Judgment on Israel and Judah</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="HOS 5:1"/><char style="add">“</char> Hear this, O priests! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 5:1">And pay attention, O house of Israel! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 5:1">And house <char style="add">is</char> toward you, turn your ear! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 5:1">Indeed unto you⁺ <char style="add">is</char> the judgment, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 5:1">because you⁺ have been a snare at Mizpah, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 5:1">and a net spread out on Tabor. <verse eid="HOS 5:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="HOS 5:2"/>And into slaughter the rebels are deep; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 5:2">and I will discipline all of them. <verse eid="HOS 5:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="HOS 5:3"/>I know Ephraim,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, the northern kingdom of Israel; also in verses 5, 9, 11, 12, 13, and 14</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 5:3">and Israel is not hidden from Me; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 5:3">for now, you engage in prositution, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 5:3">O Ephraim; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 5:3">Israel is defiled. <verse eid="HOS 5:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="HOS 5:4"/>Their deeds do not permit them </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 5:4">to return to their God; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 5:4">for the spirit of prostitution is within them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 5:4">and YHWH they do not know. <verse eid="HOS 5:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="HOS 5:5"/>And answers the pride of Israel to his face; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 5:5">and Israel and Ephraim stumble in their iniquity; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 5:5">Judah also stumbles with them. <verse eid="HOS 5:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="HOS 5:6"/>With their flocks and herds they will go </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 5:6">to seek YHWH, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 5:6">and they will not find; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 5:6">He has withdrawn from them. <verse eid="HOS 5:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="HOS 5:7"/>To YHWH they were unfaithful, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 5:7">for they have borne strange sons. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 5:7">Now the New Moon<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">their New Moon feast</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the coming month</char></note> will devour them </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 5:7">with their portions! <verse eid="HOS 5:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="HOS 5:8"/>Blow the shofar in Gibeah, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 5:8">the trumpet in Ramah! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 5:8">Give a shout <char style="add">in</char> Beth-Aven;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Beth-aven</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">house of wickedness</char><char style="ft" closed="false">. This is a derogatory term for Bethel, which means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">house of God</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see 1 Kings 12:28–29.</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 5:8">after you, O Benjamin! <verse eid="HOS 5:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="HOS 5:9"/>Ephraim will become as a desolation </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 5:9">on the day of rebuke; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 5:9">among the tribes of Israel </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 5:9">I make known what is certain. <verse eid="HOS 5:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="HOS 5:10"/>The princes of Judah have become </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 5:10">like those moving a landmark;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> See Proverbs 22:28 and Proverbs 23:10.</char></note> </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 5:10">on them I will pour out </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 5:10">my wrath like the waters. <verse eid="HOS 5:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="HOS 5:11"/>Ephraim is oppressed, crushed in judgment, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 5:11">because he was willing to walk after worthless idols.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to follow human precepts</char></note> <verse eid="HOS 5:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="HOS 5:12"/>And I <char style="add">am</char> like a moth to Ephraim, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 5:12">and like rot to the house of Judah. <verse eid="HOS 5:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="HOS 5:13"/>When Ephraim saw his sickness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 5:13">and Judah his wound, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 5:13">Ephraim went to Assyria, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 5:13">and he sent to the great king;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to King Jareb</char></note> </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 5:13">and he is not able to bring healing to you⁺, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 5:13">and he cannot remove your⁺ wound. <verse eid="HOS 5:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="HOS 5:14"/>For I <char style="add">am</char> like a lion to Ephraim, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 5:14">and like a young lion to the house of Judah. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 5:14">I—I, will tear <char style="add">them</char> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 5:14">and go away; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 5:14">I will take <char style="add">them</char>, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 5:14">and no one <char style="add">is</char> delivering. <verse eid="HOS 5:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="HOS 5:15"/>I will go—I will turn back to My place, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 5:15">until that they acknowledge their guilt and seek My face; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 5:15">in affliction they will earnestly seek Me.” <verse eid="HOS 5:15"/></para>

<chapter eid="HOS 5"/>

<chapter number="6" style="c" sid="HOS 6"/>

<para style="s">The Unrepentance of Israel and Judah</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="HOS 6:1"/>Come and let us return to YHWH, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 6:1">for He has torn <char style="add">us</char>, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 6:1">and He will heal us; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 6:1">He has struck <char style="add">us</char>, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 6:1">and He will bind us up. <verse eid="HOS 6:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="HOS 6:2"/>He will revive us after two days; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 6:2">on the third on the day He will raise us up, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 6:2">that we may live before His face. <verse eid="HOS 6:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="HOS 6:3"/>And let us know, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 6:3">let us press on to know YHWH. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 6:3">Like the dawn, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 6:3">His going forth is sure, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 6:3">and He will come like the rain to us, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 6:3">like the spring rain <char style="add">that</char> showers the earth. <verse eid="HOS 6:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="HOS 6:4"/>What will I do to you, O Ephraim?<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, the northern kingdom of Israel; also in verse 10</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 6:4">What will I do to you, O Judah? </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 6:4">And your⁺ faithfulness is like a cloud of the morning, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 6:4">and like the dew rising <char style="add">and</char> going away. <verse eid="HOS 6:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="HOS 6:5"/>Upon thus, I have hewn <char style="add">them</char> by the prophets, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 6:5">I have killed them by the words of My mouth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 6:5">and My judgments go forth <char style="add">as</char> the light! <verse eid="HOS 6:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="HOS 6:6"/>For I delight in mercy, and not sacrifice, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 6:6">and the knowledge of God </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 6:6">above burnt offerings. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Matthew 9:13 and Matthew 12:7</char></note><verse eid="HOS 6:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="HOS 6:7"/>And they, like Adam, transgressed<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">As at Adam, they transgressed</char></note> the covenant; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 6:7">there they were unfaithful with Me. <verse eid="HOS 6:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="HOS 6:8"/>Gilead <char style="add">is</char> a city of workers of iniquity, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 6:8">with a footprint of blood. <verse eid="HOS 6:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="HOS 6:9"/>Like raiders lying in wait <char style="add">for</char> a man </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 6:9"><char style="add">is</char> the band of priests; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 6:9">they murder on the way to Shechem; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 6:9">surely, they have committed wickedness. <verse eid="HOS 6:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="HOS 6:10"/>In the house of Israel </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 6:10">I have seen a horrible thing: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 6:10">There <char style="add">is</char> the prostitution of Ephraim; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 6:10">Israel is defiled. <verse eid="HOS 6:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="HOS 6:11"/>Also, O Judah, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 6:11">a harvest is set for you, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 6:11">in My turning back </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 6:11">the captivity of My people.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in My restoring the fortunes of My people</char></note> <verse eid="HOS 6:11"/></para>

<chapter eid="HOS 6"/>

<chapter number="7" style="c" sid="HOS 7"/>

<para style="s">Ephraim’s Iniquity</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="HOS 7:1"/>In My healing of Israel, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 7:1">the iniquity of Ephraim<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, the northern kingdom of Israel; also in verses 8 and 11</char></note> is uncovered, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 7:1">and the wickedness of Samaria; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 7:1">for they practice deceit, and a thief comes <char style="add">in</char>; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 7:1">bandits raid in the street. <verse eid="HOS 7:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="HOS 7:2"/>And they do not tell their hearts </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 7:2"><char style="add">that</char> all their evil I remember. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 7:2">Now their deeds have surrounded them; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 7:2">they are before My face. <verse eid="HOS 7:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="HOS 7:3"/>With their evil they make glad the king, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 7:3">and with their lies—princes. <verse eid="HOS 7:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="HOS 7:4"/>They are all adulterers, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 7:4">like an oven heated by a baker, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 7:4">who ceases stirring <char style="add">the fire</char> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 7:4">after kneading the dough until it <char style="add">is</char> leavened. <verse eid="HOS 7:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="HOS 7:5"/>On the day of our king, the princes became sick, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 7:5">raging from the wine; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 7:5">he stretched out his hand </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 7:5">with the mockers. <verse eid="HOS 7:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="HOS 7:6"/>For they approach; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 7:6">like an oven <char style="add">is</char> their heart in ambush; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 7:6">all night their baker is sleeping;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">their anger smolders</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 7:6">in the morning it burns like a fire of flame. <verse eid="HOS 7:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="HOS 7:7"/>All of them are hot like an oven, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 7:7">and they devour their judges; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 7:7">all their kings have fallen; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 7:7">no one among them calls to Me. <verse eid="HOS 7:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="HOS 7:8"/>Ephraim, he has mixed himself with the nations; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 7:8">Ephraim is a cake not turned. <verse eid="HOS 7:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="HOS 7:9"/>Strangers have devoured his power, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 7:9">and he does not know; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 7:9">even gray hairs are scattered on him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 7:9">and he does not know. <verse eid="HOS 7:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="HOS 7:10"/>And the pride of Israel testifies to his face; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 7:10">they do not return to YHWH their God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 7:10">they do not seek Him in all this. <verse eid="HOS 7:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="HOS 7:11"/>And Ephraim is like a silly dove, without sense; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 7:11">to Egypt they call; to Assyria they go. <verse eid="HOS 7:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="HOS 7:12"/>When they go, I will spread over them My net, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 7:12">like birds of the heavens I will bring them down; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 7:12">I will chastise them </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 7:12">according to the report of their congregation.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">I will chastise them when I hear them flocking together.</char></note> <verse eid="HOS 7:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="HOS 7:13"/>Woe to them, for they have fled from Me! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 7:13">Destruction <char style="add">be</char> to them, because they have transgressed against Me! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 7:13">And though I would redeem them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 7:13">they have spoken lies against Me. <verse eid="HOS 7:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="HOS 7:14"/>And they did not cry out to Me with their heart, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 7:14">when they wailed upon their beds; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 7:14">they slash themselves<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Some Hebrew manuscripts and LXX; see 1 Kings 18:28. Most Hebrew manuscripts </char><char style="fq" closed="false">They gather together</char></note> for grain and new wine; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 7:14">they rebel against Me. <verse eid="HOS 7:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="HOS 7:15"/>And I disciplined—I strengthened their arms; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 7:15">against Me they devise evil. <verse eid="HOS 7:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="HOS 7:16"/>They return, not to the Most High; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 7:16">they are like a bow of slackness; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 7:16">their princes will fall by the sword, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 7:16">from the insolence of their tongue; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 7:16">this <char style="add">is</char> their derision </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 7:16">in the land of Egypt. <verse eid="HOS 7:16"/></para>

<chapter eid="HOS 7"/>

<chapter number="8" style="c" sid="HOS 8"/>

<para style="s">Israel Will Reap the Whirlwind</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="HOS 8:1"/>To your mouth <char style="add">set</char> the shofar, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 8:1">as an eagle over the house of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 8:1">because they have transgressed My covenant, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 8:1">and against My law they have rebelled. <verse eid="HOS 8:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="HOS 8:2"/>To Me they cry, “O My God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 8:2">Israel, we know You.” <verse eid="HOS 8:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="HOS 8:3"/>Israel has rejected the good; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 8:3">an enemy will pursue him. <verse eid="HOS 8:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="HOS 8:4"/>They set up kings, and not from Me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 8:4">they made princes, and not ones I knew. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 8:4">With their silver and gold they made for themselves idols, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 8:4">that it might be cut off. <verse eid="HOS 8:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="HOS 8:5"/>He has rejected your calf,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">calf idol</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see 1 Kings 12:29.</char></note> O Samaria; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 8:5">My anger burns against them. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 8:5">Until when will they not </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 8:5">be capable of innocence? <verse eid="HOS 8:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="HOS 8:6"/>For it <char style="add">is</char> from Israel. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 8:6">A workman made it, and it <char style="add">is</char> not God. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 8:6">Surely the calf of Samaria </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 8:6">will be broken to pieces. <verse eid="HOS 8:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="HOS 8:7"/>For the wind they sow </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 8:7">and they shall reap the whirlwind. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 8:7">The stalk <char style="add">is</char> not unto it, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 8:7">a shoot not yielding flour; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 8:7">even if it should produce, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 8:7">strangers would swallow it up! <verse eid="HOS 8:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="HOS 8:8"/>Israel is swallowed up; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 8:8">now they are among the Gentiles, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 8:8">like a vessel with no delight in it. <verse eid="HOS 8:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="HOS 8:9"/>For they have gone up to Assyria; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 8:9">a wild donkey isolated by himself; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 8:9">Ephraim,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, the northern kingdom of Israel; also in verse 11</char></note> they have hired lovers. <verse eid="HOS 8:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="HOS 8:10"/>Even though they have hired among the nations, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 8:10">I will now gather them. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 8:10">And they will begin to diminish </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 8:10">from the burden of the king of princes. <verse eid="HOS 8:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="HOS 8:11"/>Because Ephraim has multiplied altars for sin, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 8:11">they have become unto him altars for sinning. <verse eid="HOS 8:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="HOS 8:12"/>Were I to write for him the myriad <char style="add">things</char> of My law, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 8:12">they would be regarded as a strange thing. <verse eid="HOS 8:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="HOS 8:13"/>The sacrifices of My gifts they sacrifice, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 8:13"><char style="add">and</char> the flesh they eat—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 8:13">YHWH does not accept them. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 8:13">Now He has in mind their iniquity, and He will attend to their sins: </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 8:13">They will return to Egypt. <verse eid="HOS 8:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="HOS 8:14"/>And Israel has forgotten his Maker and has built palaces, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 8:14">and Judah has multiplied fortified cities; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 8:14">and I will send fire upon his cities, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 8:14">and it will devour his palaces. <verse eid="HOS 8:14"/></para>

<chapter eid="HOS 8"/>

<chapter number="9" style="c" sid="HOS 9"/>

<para style="s">Israel’s Punishment</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="HOS 9:1"/>Do not be glad, O Israel, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:1">with rejoicing, like peoples. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 9:1">For you have prostitute yourself against your God; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:1">you have made love <char style="add">for</char> hire on all the floors of threshing. <verse eid="HOS 9:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="HOS 9:2"/>The threshing floor and winepress will not feed them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:2">and the new wine will fail in her. <verse eid="HOS 9:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="HOS 9:3"/>They will not dwell </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:3">in the land of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 9:3">and Ephraim<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, the northern kingdom of Israel; similarly in verses 8, 11, 13, and 16</char></note> will return to Egypt, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:3">and Assyria will eat unclean <char style="add">things</char>. <verse eid="HOS 9:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="HOS 9:4"/>They will not pour out wine to YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:4">and their sacrifices they will not be pleasng to Him—</para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 9:4">like the bread of mourners to them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:4">all those eating it will be defiled. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 9:4">For their bread <char style="add">is</char> for their own soul; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:4">it will not come <char style="add">into</char> the house of YHWH! <verse eid="HOS 9:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="HOS 9:5"/>What will you⁺ do on the day of the appointed feast, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:5">and on the day of the feast of YHWH? <verse eid="HOS 9:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="HOS 9:6"/>For behold, they go away from destruction. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:6">Egypt will gather them up, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:6"><char style="add">and</char> Memphis will bury them! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 9:6"><char style="add">And</char> the preciousness of their silver—the thistles will possess them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:6">thorns in their tents. <verse eid="HOS 9:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="HOS 9:7"/>The days of punishment have come in; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:7">the days of recompense have come in. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:7">let Israel knows </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 9:7">the prophet <char style="add">is</char> a fool, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:7">the man of the spirit is insane </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 9:7">over the abundance of your iniquity, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:7">and the greatness of your hatred. <verse eid="HOS 9:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="HOS 9:8"/>The prophet, with my God, <char style="add">is</char> the one watching Ephraim;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">The prophet is the watchman over Ephraim, the people of my God</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:8">a snare of a fowler <char style="add">is</char> on all his paths; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:8">hostility <char style="add">is</char> in the house of his God. <verse eid="HOS 9:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="HOS 9:9"/>They have sunk deep, corrupting themselves, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:9">as in the days of Gibeah; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 9:9">He will remember their iniquity; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:9">He will attend to their sins. <verse eid="HOS 9:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="HOS 9:10"/>Like grapes in the wilderness, I found Israel; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:10">as the firstfruits on the fig tree in its first season, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:10">I saw your⁺ fathers. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 9:10">They went <char style="add">to</char> Baal-peor </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:10">and dedicated themselves to that shame, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 9:10">and they became as detestable </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:10">as that which they loved! <verse eid="HOS 9:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="HOS 9:11"/>Ephraim, like a bird, their glory will fly away </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:11">from the birth and from the belly and from conceiving. <verse eid="HOS 9:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="HOS 9:12"/>Even if they bring up their sons, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:12">I will bereave them of each man. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 9:12">Yes indeed, woe to them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:12">at My turning away from them! <verse eid="HOS 9:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="HOS 9:13"/>Ephraim, as I have seen, like Tyre, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:13">is planted in a pleasant place; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 9:13">and Ephraim will bring out </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:13">his children to one who slaughters. <verse eid="HOS 9:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="HOS 9:14"/>Give to them, O YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:14">what will You give? </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 9:14">Give to them a womb miscarrying, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:14">and breasts <char style="add">that are</char> dry. <verse eid="HOS 9:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="HOS 9:15"/>All their evil <char style="add">is</char> in Gilgal, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:15">for there I came to hate them, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 9:15">because of the evil of their deeds, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:15">I will drive them out from My house. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 9:15">I will not continue to love them; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:15">all their princes <char style="add">are</char> rebellious. <verse eid="HOS 9:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="HOS 9:16"/>Ephraim is stricken, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:16">their root has withered; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:16">they will not bear fruit. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 9:16">Even if they give birth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:16">I will kill the precious ones of their womb. <verse eid="HOS 9:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="HOS 9:17"/>My God will reject them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:17">because they did not listen to Him, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 9:17">and they will be wanderers </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 9:17">among the nations. <verse eid="HOS 9:17"/></para>

<chapter eid="HOS 9"/>

<chapter number="10" style="c" sid="HOS 10"/>

<para style="s">Retribution for Israel’s Sin</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="HOS 10:1"/>Israel <char style="add">was</char> a luxuriant vine; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 10:1">he set forth fruit for himself. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 10:1">With the increase of his fruit, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 10:1">he made an increase of the altars; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 10:1">according to the richness of his land, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 10:1">they made rich the sacred pillars. <verse eid="HOS 10:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="HOS 10:2"/>Their heart has been divided, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 10:2">now they are guilty; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 10:2">He will break down their altars; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 10:2">He will demolish their sacred pillars. <verse eid="HOS 10:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="HOS 10:3"/>For now they say, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 10:3">“There is no king for us, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 10:3">because we did not fear YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 10:3">and <char style="add">as for</char> the king, what could he do for us?” <verse eid="HOS 10:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="HOS 10:4"/>They have spoken words, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 10:4">swearing falsely <char style="add">in</char> cutting a covenant, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 10:4">and judgment sprouts up like a poison </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 10:4">in the furrows of the field. <verse eid="HOS 10:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="HOS 10:5"/>For the calf of Beth-aven<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Beth-aven</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">house of wickedness</char><char style="ft" closed="false">. This is a derogatory term for Bethel, which means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">house of God</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see 1 Kings 12:28–29.</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 10:5">those dwelling in Samaria fear; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 10:5">indeed its people mourn over it, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 10:5">and its idolatrous priests who rejoiced over it, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 10:5">over its glory </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 10:5">that has departed from it. <verse eid="HOS 10:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="HOS 10:6"/>Also it will be carried along to Assyria </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 10:6">as tribute to the great king;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to King Jareb</char></note> </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 10:6">Ephraim<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, the northern kingdom of Israel; also in verse 11</char></note> will receive shame, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 10:6">and Israel will be ashamed of his idol.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of its own counsel</char></note> <verse eid="HOS 10:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="HOS 10:7"/>Samaria will be cut off <char style="add">with</char> her king, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 10:7">like a twig on the face of the water. <verse eid="HOS 10:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="HOS 10:8"/>The high places of Aven will be destroyed, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 10:8">and the sin of Israel; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 10:8">the thorn and thistle will come up over their altars, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 10:8">and they will say to the mountains, “Cover us!” </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 10:8">And to the hills, “Fall on us!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of wickedness</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Aven</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is a reference to Beth-aven (a derogatory term for Bethel); see verse 5.</char></note>” <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Luke 23:30; see also Revelation 6:16.</char></note><verse eid="HOS 10:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="HOS 10:9"/>From the days of Gibeah, you have sinned, O Israel. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 10:9">There they have stood. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 10:9">Did it not overtake them in Gibeah—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 10:9">the battle against the sons of iniquity?<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Did not the battle overtake the sons of iniquity in Gibeah?</char></note> <verse eid="HOS 10:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="HOS 10:10"/>When I desire, I will discipline them; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 10:10">and peoples will be gathered against them, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 10:10">at My disciplining them </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 10:10">for the two of their transgressions. <verse eid="HOS 10:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="HOS 10:11"/>And Ephraim <char style="add">is</char> a trained heifer, loving to thresh; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 10:11">and I passed over upon her fair neck; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 10:11">I will drive Ephraim; Judah will plow; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 10:11">Jacob will harrow for him. <verse eid="HOS 10:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="HOS 10:12"/>Sow for yourselves unto righteousness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 10:12"><char style="add">and</char> reap to the mouth of loving devotion; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 10:12">break up for yourself the fallow ground, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 10:12">for <char style="add">it is</char> time to seek YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 10:12">until He should come </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 10:12">and shower righteousness upon you⁺. <verse eid="HOS 10:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="HOS 10:13"/>You⁺ have plowed wickedness; you⁺ have reaped injustice; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 10:13">you⁺ have eaten the fruit of lies. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 10:13">Because you trusted in your own way, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 10:13">in the multitude of your mighty men, <verse eid="HOS 10:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="HOS 10:14"/>therefore will arise an uproar among your people, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 10:14">and all your fortresses will be destroyed, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 10:14">like the destruction of Shalman <char style="add">in</char> Beth-arbel </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 10:14">on the day of battle, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 10:14">when a mother upon <char style="add">her</char> children </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 10:14">was dashed to pieces. <verse eid="HOS 10:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="HOS 10:15"/>So may He do to you⁺, O Bethel, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 10:15">from the face of your⁺ great evil; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 10:15">at dawn he will be utterly cut off—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 10:15">the king of Israel! <verse eid="HOS 10:15"/></para>

<chapter eid="HOS 10"/>

<chapter number="11" style="c" sid="HOS 11"/>

<para style="s">Out of Egypt I Called My Son</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="HOS 11:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Matthew 2:13–15</char></note>When Israel <char style="add">was</char> a child, I loved him; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 11:1">and out of Egypt I called My son.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Matthew 2:15</char></note> <verse eid="HOS 11:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="HOS 11:2"/>And I called to them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 11:2">so they went away from My face;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX; Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">They called them, so they went away from their faces</char></note> </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 11:2">to the Baals they sacrificed, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 11:2">and to the carved images they burned incense. <verse eid="HOS 11:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="HOS 11:3"/>And I had guided the feet of Ephraim,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, the northern kingdom of Israel; also in verses 8, 9, and 12</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 11:3">taking them by the arms; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 11:3">they did not know </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 11:3">that <char style="add">it was</char> I <char style="add">who</char> healed them. <verse eid="HOS 11:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="HOS 11:4"/>With cords of humanity I drew them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 11:4">with bands of love; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 11:4">and I was to them like those lifting the yoke up <char style="add">from</char> their jaws, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 11:4">and I bent down to them to let <char style="add">them</char> eat. <verse eid="HOS 11:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="HOS 11:5"/>He will not return to the land of Egypt, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 11:5">and Assyria—it will be his king, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 11:5">because they refused to return. <verse eid="HOS 11:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="HOS 11:6"/>And the sword will twist through his cities, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 11:6">and will finish off his bars, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 11:6">and will devour their counseling! <verse eid="HOS 11:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="HOS 11:7"/>And My people are bent on turning away from Me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 11:7">though to the Most High they call <char style="add">to</char> Him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 11:7">He will not at all exalt them. <verse eid="HOS 11:7"/></para>

<para style="s">God’s Love for Israel</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="HOS 11:8"/>How can I give you up, O Ephraim? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 11:8">Can I deliver you up, O Israel? </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 11:8">How can I make you like Admah? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 11:8">Can I make you like Zeboiim? </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 11:8">My heart is turned over within Me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 11:8">together My compassions are kindled. <verse eid="HOS 11:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="HOS 11:9"/>I will not act <char style="add">in</char> the burning of My anger; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 11:9">I will not turn back to destroy Ephraim. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 11:9">For I <char style="add">am</char> God, and not a man—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 11:9">the Holy One in your midst, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 11:9">and I will not come in enmity. <verse eid="HOS 11:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="HOS 11:10"/>After YHWH they shall walk; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 11:10">like a lion He will roar; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 11:10">when He roars, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 11:10">the sons from the west will come trembling. <verse eid="HOS 11:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="HOS 11:11"/>They will come trembling like a bird from Egypt, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 11:11">and like a dove from the land of Assyria, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 11:11">and I will let them dwell in their homes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 11:11">a declaration of YHWH. <verse eid="HOS 11:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="HOS 11:12"/>Ephraim has surrounded Me with lies, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 11:12">and the house of Israel with deceit, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 11:12">and Judah still wanders restlessly with God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 11:12">and with the holy ones is faithful.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and Judah is unruly against God, the faithful Holy One</char></note> <verse eid="HOS 11:12"/></para>

<chapter eid="HOS 11"/>

<chapter number="12" style="c" sid="HOS 12"/>

<para style="s">A Reproof of Ephraim, Judah, and Jacob</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="HOS 12:1"/>Ephraim<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, the northern kingdom of Israel; also in verses 8 and 14</char></note> is grazing <char style="add">on</char> the wind </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 12:1">and pursuing the east wind all the day, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 12:1">he multiplies lies and violence; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 12:1">they cut a covenant with Assyria </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 12:1">and oil is carried to Egypt. <verse eid="HOS 12:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="HOS 12:2"/>A dispute <char style="add">is</char> unto YHWH against Judah, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 12:2">to visit punishment on Jacob<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Jacob</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">he grasps the heel</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">he deceives</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> according to his ways; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 12:2">according to his deeds He will recompense to him. <verse eid="HOS 12:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="HOS 12:3"/>In the womb he took his brother by the heel, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 12:3">and in his strength he struggled with God. <verse eid="HOS 12:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="HOS 12:4"/>He struggled with the angel<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Angel</char></note> and prevailed; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 12:4">he wept and sought favor from Him; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 12:4">at Bethel he found Him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 12:4">and there He spoke with Him,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX and Syriac; MT </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and there He spoke with us</char></note> <verse eid="HOS 12:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="HOS 12:5"/>and YHWH, God of Hosts—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 12:5">YHWH <char style="add">is</char> His memorial. <verse eid="HOS 12:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="HOS 12:6"/>And you must return to your God; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 12:6">Keep love and justice, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 12:6">and wait for your God continually! <verse eid="HOS 12:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="HOS 12:7"/>A Canaanite<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">a merchant </char></note> <char style="add">has</char> scales of deceit in his hand; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 12:7">he loves to oppress. <verse eid="HOS 12:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="HOS 12:8"/>And Ephraim said, “Surely I have become rich. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 12:8">I have found wealth for myself. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 12:8">In all my labors they will find in me </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 12:8">no iniquity that <char style="add">is</char> sin.” <verse eid="HOS 12:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="HOS 12:9"/>And I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH your God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 12:9">from the land of Egypt; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 12:9">again I will make you dwell in tents, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 12:9">as in the days of the appointed feast. <verse eid="HOS 12:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="HOS 12:10"/>And I have spoken by the prophets, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 12:10">and I have multiplied visions, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 12:10">and by the hand of the prophets I have given parables. <verse eid="HOS 12:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="HOS 12:11"/>If iniquity <char style="add">is</char> in Gilead, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 12:11">surely they are worthless; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 12:11">In Gilgal they sacrifice bulls; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 12:11">even their altars <char style="add">are</char> as heaps </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 12:11">over the furrows of the field. <verse eid="HOS 12:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="HOS 12:12"/>And Jacob fled to the land of Aram,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, northwest Mesopotamia</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 12:12">and Israel worked for a wife, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 12:12">and for a wife he tended. <verse eid="HOS 12:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="HOS 12:13"/>And by a prophet YHWH brought up Israel from Egypt, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 12:13">and by a prophet he was kept. <verse eid="HOS 12:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="HOS 12:14"/>Ephraim has provoked to anger bitterly, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 12:14">and his bloodguilt He will leave upon him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 12:14">and his reproach his Lord will make return to him. <verse eid="HOS 12:14"/></para>

<chapter eid="HOS 12"/>

<chapter number="13" style="c" sid="HOS 13"/>

<para style="s">God’s Anger against Israel</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="HOS 13:1"/>When Ephraim<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, the northern kingdom of Israel; also in verse 12</char></note> spoke <char style="add">there was</char> trembling; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 13:1">he was exalted in Israel, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 13:1">and he became guilty by the Baal, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 13:1">and he died. <verse eid="HOS 13:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="HOS 13:2"/>And now they add to sin, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 13:2">and have made for themselves molten images </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 13:2">idols from their silver according to their skill, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 13:2">the work of craftsmen, all of them. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 13:2">They say of them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 13:2">“Those who sacrifice man, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 13:2">they will kiss the calves.”<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">“The men who sacrifice will kiss the calves!”</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> See 1 Kings 19:18.</char></note> <verse eid="HOS 13:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="HOS 13:3"/>Therefore they will be like the cloud of morning, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 13:3">and like the dew rising early that passes away, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 13:3">like chaff that swirls from the threshing floor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 13:3">and like smoke from a window. <verse eid="HOS 13:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="HOS 13:4"/>For I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH your God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 13:4">from the land of Egypt; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 13:4">and you know no gods besides Me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 13:4">and no one is able to save besides Me! <verse eid="HOS 13:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="HOS 13:5"/>I knew you in the wilderness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 13:5">in the land of drought. <verse eid="HOS 13:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="HOS 13:6"/>At their grazing, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 13:6">they became satisfied; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 13:6">they were filled, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 13:6">and their heart was exalted; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 13:6">upon thus they forgot Me! <verse eid="HOS 13:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="HOS 13:7"/>And I will become to them like a lion; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 13:7">like a leopard alongside the pathway I will watch. <verse eid="HOS 13:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="HOS 13:8"/>I will encounter them like a bear bereaved, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 13:8">and I will tear open the enclosure of their heart; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 13:8">there I will devour them like a lion; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 13:8">a beast of the field will tear them apart. <verse eid="HOS 13:8"/></para>

<para style="s">Death and Resurrection1 Corinthians 15:50–58</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="HOS 13:9"/>He has destroyed you, O Israel, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 13:9">for <char style="add">you are</char> against Me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 13:9">against your helper! <verse eid="HOS 13:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="HOS 13:10"/>Where <char style="add">is</char> your king now,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Shall I be your King now</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 13:10">that he may save you in all your cities? </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 13:10">And your rulers of whom you said, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 13:10">“Give to me a king and princes”? <verse eid="HOS 13:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="HOS 13:11"/>I gave to you a king in My anger, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 13:11">and I took <char style="add">him</char> away in My wrath. <verse eid="HOS 13:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="HOS 13:12"/>The iniquity of Ephraim is bound up; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 13:12">his sin is stored up. <verse eid="HOS 13:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="HOS 13:13"/>The pains of childbirth will come to him; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 13:13">he <char style="add">is</char> not a wise a son, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 13:13">for he would not stand </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 13:13">at the time for the breaking forth of sons. <verse eid="HOS 13:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="HOS 13:14"/>I will ransom them from the hand of Sheol; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 13:14">will I redeem them from death. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 13:14">Where <char style="add">are</char> your plagues, O Death? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 13:14">Where <char style="add">is</char> is your destruction, O Grave?<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Shall I ransom them from the power of Sheol? Shall I redeem them from Death?</char></note> </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 13:14">Compassion is hidden from My eyes! <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Where, O Death, is your penalty? Where, O Hades, is your sting?</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in 1 Corinthians 15:55</char></note><verse eid="HOS 13:14"/></para>

<para style="s">Judgment on Samaria</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="HOS 13:15"/>Though he is fruitful among <char style="add">his</char> brothers </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 13:15">an east wind will come, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 13:15">the wind of YHWH! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 13:15">From the desert <char style="add">it is</char> coming up, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 13:15">and his fountain will become dry, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 13:15">and his spring will dry out; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 13:15">it will plunder the treasure </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 13:15">of every article of desire. <verse eid="HOS 13:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="HOS 13:16"/>Samaria is guilty, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 13:16">for she has rebelled against her God. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 13:16">They will fall by the sword; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 13:16">their infants will be dashed to pieces, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 13:16">and their pregnant women ripped open. <verse eid="HOS 13:16"/></para>

<chapter eid="HOS 13"/>

<chapter number="14" style="c" sid="HOS 14"/>

<para style="s">A Call to Repentance</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="HOS 14:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Zechariah 1:1–6</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Jeremiah 3:11–25</char></note>So return, O Israel, to YHWH your God! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 14:1">For you have stumbled by your iniquity. <verse eid="HOS 14:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="HOS 14:2"/>Take with you⁺ words, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 14:2">and return to YHWH. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 14:2">Say to Him: “Lift away all iniquity, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 14:2">and receive what is good, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 14:2">and we offer </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 14:2">the fruit of our lips.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX and Syriac; Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and we offer the calves of our lips</char></note> <verse eid="HOS 14:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="HOS 14:3"/>Assyria cannot save us; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 14:3">we will not ride on horses, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 14:3">and we will not say anymore, ‘Our gods’ </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 14:3">to the work of our hands. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 14:3">For in You the fatherless find compassion.” <verse eid="HOS 14:3"/></para>

<para style="s">A Promise of God’s Blessing</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="HOS 14:4"/>I will heal their backsliding, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 14:4">I will love them willingly; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 14:4">for My anger has turned back from him. <verse eid="HOS 14:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="HOS 14:5"/>I will be like the dew to Israel; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 14:5">he will blossom like the lily, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 14:5">and he will strike forth his roots like Lebanon. <verse eid="HOS 14:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="HOS 14:6"/>His branches will go forth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 14:6">and his beauty will be like the olive tree, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 14:6">and the fragrance unto him like Lebanon. <verse eid="HOS 14:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="HOS 14:7"/>Those dwelling in his shade will return; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 14:7">they will revive like the grain and blossom like the vine; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 14:7">his memorial <char style="add">is</char> as wine of Lebanon. <verse eid="HOS 14:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="HOS 14:8"/>O Ephraim,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, the northern kingdom of Israel</char></note> what <char style="add">is</char> unto me </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 14:8">anymore with idols? </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 14:8">I have answered and have watched over him. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 14:8">I <char style="add">am</char> luxuriant like a cypress;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">pine</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">juniper</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">fir</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 14:8">your fruit is found in Me. <verse eid="HOS 14:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="HOS 14:9"/>Who <char style="add">is</char> wise? Let him understand these <char style="add">things</char>. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 14:9"><char style="add">Who is</char> understanding? Let him know them. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="HOS 14:9">For straight <char style="add">are</char> the ways of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 14:9">and the righteous walk in them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="HOS 14:9">and transgressors stumble in them. <verse eid="HOS 14:9"/></para>

<chapter eid="HOS 14"/>

</usx>
